Plan for 0006-set-logged  (digest 6f7042762561…)

-- transaction group 1 ---------------- atomic --
 0. set_logged
    LOCK TABLE "shop"."orders" IN SHARE UPDATE EXCLUSIVE MODE;
    ALTER TABLE "shop"."orders" SET LOGGED;
    lock: AccessExclusiveLock on shop.orders for the whole rewrite
    why:  measured: this REWRITES the table -- relfilenode changes in both directions -- so 2.0 GiB is copied under an exclusive lock, and every byte of it is written to WAL as it goes. SHARE UPDATE EXCLUSIVE is taken first: it waits out an autovacuum without queueing reads or writes, and the exclusive lock after it is asked for with a short timeout and retried
    time: no statement timeout: it takes as long as the table is large, and statement_timeout_ms is lifted for it

 warn: SET LOGGED writes the entire table to WAL as it rewrites it, so a replica must receive 2.0 GiB of WAL and archiving must absorb it. On a large table that is the dominant cost, and it lands on the replication link rather than on this connection.
